# =====================================================================================
# JaoKob · .gitignore
# Part A is active now. Part B is the production blueprint: every rule is commented out
# on purpose so agents and security tools can still read these files during Sprint 5.
# =====================================================================================

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------
# Part A · Active rules (development hygiene)
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------

# Operating-system metadata
.DS_Store
**/.DS_Store

# Local secrets and machine-specific configuration
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# Generated development and deployment artifacts
node_modules/
coverage/
_site/
output/playwright/
*.log

# Python bytecode from local verification scripts, and Blender auto-backups
__pycache__/
*.pyc
*.blend1

# Local agent worktrees and personal agent settings (never part of the project)
.claude/worktrees/
.claude/settings.local.json

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------
# Part B · Production release blueprint (ALL COMMENTED, CR-20261031-0420)
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------
#
# When to use: on the PO's release sign-off day, before the repository is shown publicly
# as the finished game.
#
# The playable game itself is already safe: GitHub Pages ships only the explicit allowlist in
# specs/releases/*.json (index.html, src/, assets/). These rules are about what the public can
# browse in the repository.
#
# How to apply (three steps; uncommenting alone is not enough):
#   1. Uncomment the blocks you want below.
#   2. Untrack what is already committed while keeping your local copies, for example:
#        git rm -r --cached docs/dialogue docs/design-system/ux-mockups
#   3. Commit on develop, review, then merge to main.
# Files stay in the Git history after this. Removing them from history is a separate,
# destructive decision (history rewrite and force push) that needs explicit PO approval.
#
# Keep public in every case: README.md, LICENSE files, index.html, src/, the shipped assets/,
# specs/, tests/unit/ and the credits or licence text that the shipped assets require.

# --- B1 · Story spoilers: the full five-act script, every branch and all three endings -------
# The game is a gift; anyone reading these files before playing would know every ending.
# docs/design-system/five-act-narrative-gameplay-master-plan.md
# docs/design-system/act*-living-keepsake-rewrite-blueprint.md
# docs/design-system/new-five-act-story-and-mechanics-proposal.md
# docs/archive/design-system-pre-adr032/

# --- B2 · Multi-agent collaboration records ---------------------------------------------------
# Internal conversations between AI agents and the PO; working notes, not product.
# docs/dialogue/
# .agents/

# --- B3 · Raw AI generation records and image-prompt pipelines ---------------------------------
# Raw prompts, generation logs and job lists. Before enabling, publish a short credits or licence
# summary for every shipped asset, because assets/provenance/ is also the licensing evidence.
# assets/provenance/*.json
# docs/design-system/asset-prompts/

# --- B4 · Unapproved image candidates -----------------------------------------------------------
# Every versions/vN/ folder holds candidates; the approved file is promoted to the canonical path
# without a version number. Check that nothing in specs/releases/ points into versions/ first.
# assets/images/**/versions/
# assets/images/asset-manifest-v*.json

# --- B5 · Internal review pages, mockups and verification harnesses ----------------------------
# docs/design-system/ux-mockups/
# docs/design-system/evidence/*.html
# docs/design-system/evidence/*-verification.json
# docs/design-system/evidence/*-doc-checks.json
# docs/design-system/evidence/*-browser-review.json
# docs/design-system/evidence/*-unit-summary.txt

# --- B6 · Research spikes, 3D source models and raw inbox --------------------------------------
# docs/proposals/3d-keepsake-spike/
# docs/raw/
# *.blend
# *.glb

# --- B7 · Browser test evidence (screenshots and state dumps) -----------------------------------
# tests/e2e/evidence/

# --- B8 · Planning history -----------------------------------------------------------------------
# Optional: keep these public if the repository should show how the game was built.
# docs/archive/
# docs/proposals/
# docs/rfc/
